  "body": "Wanted: the Tormach plasma post (`tormach-plasma.cps`) writes more work offsets and the end-unit word.\n- Today `workOffsetMax = 6`. The post refuses offsets 7-9 (`G59.1`-`G59.3`) and `G54.1 P<n>`. The 1300PL control (PathPilot) supports them.\n- The post declares no `endUnits`, so the engine refuses the `EndUnits` option.\n\nEvidence (upstream/main `1c0152c91`):\n- `assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps:23`: `workOffsetMax = 6`; `:141` refuses higher offsets.\n- `crates/post/src/post/end_units.rs:5-6` and `refusal()`.\n- Tormach 1300PL operator's manuals UM10720 (pp. 11, 61, 94, 105) and UM10770 (pp. 46, 59-60).\n\nFound by the post audit against the Tormach manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means:\n- Offsets 7-9 post as `G59.1`-`G59.3`, and higher offsets as `G54.1 P<n>`. Golden tests pin one of each.\n- The post declares `endUnits`, and a test pins the end-unit word before `M30`.\n",
